{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeDsfykSnbt2968HSsg4a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UxHbMaiPWvBugrSpDFer7N","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p3.txt <<'EOF'\n1.3: the `lim <= topk` early-out is bit-exact, 22 % faster in the kernel, and worth nothing\n\nLadder item 1.3, closed as a MEASURED NULL rather than a win. The change is real: below ctx 2048\nevery candidate is already in the top-k, and `topk_radix_select` was spending a whole radix level\n(256-bin clear, a strided pass with a shared atomicAdd per survivor, a serial scan on thread 0)\ndiscovering that. Skipping it is provably identical output — the threshold it would have computed\nis <= every candidate's composite, so `thr = 0` selects the same set — and standalone it is worth\n+2.1 to +4.1 us per call at T <= 512, +0.00 +/- 0.03 us above it.\n\nIn situ it is 0.07 % of a forward, and that was pre-registered in the script header before the run:\n21 ratio-4 layers x ~4 us = 0.085 ms of a ~130 ms step.\n\nMEASURED, paired, OFF arm first so drift penalises the early-out, 34/34 legs byte-identical in\ngenerated token ids, tau identical to three decimals on every leg:\n\n  ctx 6248 control  147.45 -> 147.69  (+0.24)   <- T=1565, early CANNOT fire: identical code\n  ctx 6260 sweep    144.48 -> 144.83  (+0.35)   <- likewise\n  ctx 1656 control  141.17 -> 141.11  (-0.06)\n  ctx 1664 sweep    135.72 -> 135.81  (+0.10)\n  ctx  889 sweep    131.72 -> 131.83  (+0.11)\n  ctx  492 sweep    126.86 -> 126.33  (-0.53)\n  ctx  249 sweep    127.29 -> 127.08  (-0.21)\n\n  b = 3.008 +/- 0.241 -> 3.036 +/- 0.240   (2.977 -> 3.006 width-controlled); a = 127.92 -> 127.84\n\nThe two ctx-6144 legs are the point: both arms run provably identical code there and still differed\nby +0.24 and +0.35 ms, so the null is stated against a zero measured INSIDE the experiment rather\nthan against a 3.5 % spread quoted from another day. i:topk, the only mark that brackets the changed\nlaunch, did see it: 0.42 -> 0.28 ms at ctx 768, 0.52 -> 0.34 at 1536, 0.72 -> 0.72 at 6144.\n\nKEPT, default on (`DSV4_TOPK_EARLY=0` restores the full search), because it is strictly less work\nfor identical output. Gates: unit gate over 4 kernel shapes x 13 lengths x 6 distributions with the\nearly-out both ON and OFF; in-situ DSV4_TOPK_GATE memcmp, 125 PASS / 0 FAIL over 7,808 checks and\n66,972,918 index slots; standing argmax GATE; LOSSLESS gate at tau 2.87.\n\nWHAT IT MEANS, which is worth more than the item. 1.3 was ranked above 1.5 on 0.4's attribution of\ni:topk at 13.47 ms at ctx 12,288. 1.2 took i:topk to 0.72 ms one iteration earlier, so this was\nbuilt against a headroom that no longer existed and nobody re-derived it. A ranked work list is a\nfunction of a cost model and the item above it just changed the cost model. New ladder rule 6:\nre-attribute before you pick — it is free, because every A/B here already runs a dprof pair.\n\nRule 7 is its counterweight, from the near-miss it caused. This iteration's re-attribution fits\ncattn:sparse at 1.694 +/- 0.065 ms/1000 against 0.4's 0.709 +/- 0.050 — which taken at face value\npromotes item 1.7 above 1.5. It is one concave curve read over two windows: per-point medians run\n9.35/15.72/19.89 ms at ctx 768/1536/6144 and 19.22/19.90/21.17 at 3072/6144/12,288, i.e. 8.29 ms per\n1000 across the first leg and 0.208 across the last, which is a top-k gather saturating once context\nexceeds k x ratio. i:score over the same samples is 0.88/1.25/3.53 = 0.482 then 0.495 per 1000,\ngenuinely linear. The ladder order stands and 1.5 is still the next kernel.\n\nWiki, same commit: negative-results.md §4c (adopted, bit-exact, worth nothing — and why it was\nbuilt), measurement-and-traps.md §15 (put a leg the change cannot touch inside the same sweep) and\n§16 (a fitted slope is only ms/1000 if the mark is linear), context-scaling.md (1.3 status and the\npost-1.2 re-attribution table), kernel-optimisations.md §2.6 (cross-reference), README.md state\ntable — where 1.3 appears as a blank on purpose.\n\nEvidence: evidence/decode_loop/{fit_1p3_paired,fit_1p3_on,fit_1p3_off,fit_1p3_itopk}.txt,\ngate_topk_radix_1p3.log, server_1p3_gate.log, dprof_ctx_1p3_{on,off}.txt,\ndecode_1p3_lossless.log, topk_early_ab.log.\nEOF\necho written; ls -la evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p3.txt","description":"Write the prepared commit message"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":446,"cache_read_input_tokens":98888,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":446},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16d3a2cb-0895-4089-9bd7-f8432e10d535","uuid":"06dfb6bb-e8b5-4e0f-8115-fd7722624c10","timestamp":"2026-08-20T10:52:59.873Z","request_id":"req_011CeDsfxs7oCLzAfZTbbNi8"}
