{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeDsiDNYognZkmxB8C3oX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration 4 done. Item **1.3** is closed as a measured null.\n\n## What I found\n\nIteration 3 had already built and measured 1.3 — code, gates, paired A/B, dprof pair, all committed in `b9334a4` — but ran out of time before the write-up, so the item sat unchecked with no decision. This iteration reproduced the unit gate first-hand, made the keep/revert call, and wrote it up.\n\n## The measurement\n\nThe kernel change is real. Below ctx 2048 every candidate is already in the top-k, and `topk_radix_select` was burning a whole radix level to discover that. Skipping it is **+2.1 to +4.1 µs per call at T ≤ 512, +0.00 ± 0.03 µs above it** (reproduced this iteration).\n\nEnd-to-end it is nothing, and the script's header said so before the run: 21 ratio-4 layers × ~4 µs = 0.085 ms of a ~130 ms forward = **0.07 %**.\n\n| ctx | fires | before | after | delta | tau b/a |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 6248 / 6260 | **no — identical code** | 147.45 / 144.48 | 147.69 / 144.83 | **+0.24 / +0.35** | unchanged |\n| 1656 / 1664 / 889 / 492 / 249 | yes | — | — | −0.06 / +0.10 / +0.11 / −0.53 / −0.21 | unchanged |\n\n`b = 3.008 ± 0.241 → 3.036 ± 0.240`. 34/34 legs byte-identical token ids; tau identical to three decimals on every leg. The two ctx-6144 legs run provably identical code in both arms and still differed by +0.24 and +0.35 ms — so the null is stated against a zero measured *inside* the experiment. `i:topk` (the only mark bracketing the changed launch) saw it: **0.42 → 0.28 ms at ctx 768, 0.52 → 0.34 at 1536, 0.72 → 0.72 at 6144**.\n\n**Kept, default on.** Bit-exact across four gates (unit gate with the early-out both ON and OFF; in-situ memcmp 125 PASS / 0 FAIL over 7,808 checks and 66.9 M index slots; standing argmax GATE; LOSSLESS at tau 2.87), and strictly less work. Filed as a null, not a win.\n\n## The part worth more than the item\n\n1.3 was ranked where it was because `i:topk` measured 13.47 ms at ctx 12,288. **1.2 took it to 0.72 ms one iteration earlier** — so 1.3 was built against headroom that had ceased to exist, and nobody re-derived it. New ladder rule 6: re-attribute before you pick; it's free, because every A/B already runs a dprof pair.\n\nRule 7 is its counterweight, from the near-miss that produced it. The fresh attribution fits `cattn:sparse` at 1.694 ± 0.065 against 0.4's 0.709 ± 0.050 — which at face value promotes item 1.7 over 1.5. It's one concave curve read over two windows (8.29 ms/1000 across the first leg, 0.208 across the last — a top-k gather saturating once ctx exceeds k×ratio). `i:score` over the same samples is 0.482 then 0.495 per 1000, genuinely linear. **The ladder order stands; 1.5 is still the next kernel.**\n\nWiki, same commit: `negative-results.md` §4c, `measurement-and-traps.md` §15–16, `context-scaling.md` (1.3 status + re-attribution table), `kernel-optimisations.md` §2.6 cross-ref, and the README state table — where 1.3 appears as a blank on purpose.\n\n`COMMIT_MSG_1p3.txt` is written for the driver to commit and push (git writes are denied to me by `.claude/settings.json`). Next unchecked item is **1.4** at line 595."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":628,"cache_read_input_tokens":101395,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":628},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16d3a2cb-0895-4089-9bd7-f8432e10d535","uuid":"1452e9ef-81fc-41b4-b55a-97f8f30ced40","timestamp":"2026-08-20T10:53:22.920Z","request_id":"req_011CeDsiCKYyfSric1vvy6HK"}
